 "lessons": [
  "A template label like '(if applicable)' or 'optional' marks a conditional rule. Ask when it applies instead of writing 'always include' from outputs that all include it.",
  "Source limits are often stated in another unit (characters, not words) or for a narrower span (caption body, not caption plus hashtags). Measure several units and report a loose range, not the tight observed band.",
  "Tone words per channel (professional, conversational) and process advice (research hashtags, use native features, format for mobile) leave weak traces. List them as probes to confirm.",
  "Exact counts seen in every output (3 hashtags, 5 hashtags, 18-19 tags) often sit inside a wider allowed range. Write 'up to N' or 'N to M' and flag the range as unconfirmed."
 ]
